# managed by Ansible — nut role (master)
# Listen on loopback + the nas Home-VLAN IP (intra-VLAN to clients on VLAN 10).
#
# A LISTEN line is only half of a remote leg: exposure = the addresses you LISTEN on, privilege
# = upsd.users. ACCEPT/REJECT are ignored by the installed NUT — never re-add them to "narrow".
# upsd binds each LISTEN once at start-up, so the address must be configured before it starts:
# the network-online drop-in + prove-bind-and-repair task in tasks/main.yml keep a silent miss.
# → docs/hardware-ups.md §Monitoring & shutdown — implementation state
# What the open port gives a Home-VLAN peer is bounded: an
# unauthenticated `GET VAR` reads NOTHING back (upsd answers no data before LOGIN), so the
# exposure is an open TCP port + a connection slot out of MAXCONN, not a data leak.
# The listen address derives from `network_static_hosts` (CONVENTIONS §2 — no literals).
LISTEN 127.0.0.1 3493
LISTEN {{ nut_listen_ip }} 3493
MAXCONN 16
